desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Detect Insecure Websocket"
	title_zh: "检测到不安全的 WebSocket 连接",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-detect-insecure-websocket"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `detect-insecure-websocket` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/javascript/lang/security/detect-insecure-websocket.yaml).
Original message: Insecure WebSocket Detected. WebSocket Secure (wss) should be used for all WebSocket connections.

CWE: CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information
References:
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures
Note: context-aware regex — ws:// hits are dropped when inside ws://localhost.* / ws://127.0.0.1.* regions (pattern-not-inside).
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Use wss:// (WebSocket Secure) for all WebSocket connections.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.js": <<<POS
var scheme = "ws://";
var uri = scheme + window.document.location.host + "/";
var ws = new WebSocket(uri);
YAKLANG_SF_POS_source-detect-insecure-websocket
ws://foo/bar
POS
	"safefile://neg.js": <<<NEG
var secure_url = "wss://my/url";
var localhost = "ws://localhost:27017/freecodecamp?directConnection=true";
var local = "ws://127.0.0.1:3000"
NEG
)

${*}.pattern_regex(/\bws:\/\//) as $t
${*}.pattern_regex(/\bws:\/\/localhost.*/) as $j1
${*}.pattern_regex(/\bws:\/\/127\.0\.0\.1.*/) as $j2
$t not_inside $j1 as $a
$a not_inside $j2 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Detect Insecure Websocket",
	title_zh: "检测到不安全的 WebSocket 连接",
	message: "Insecure WebSocket Detected. WebSocket Secure (wss) should be used for all WebSocket connections.",
}
